server_name repo.example.com www.repo.example.com;

Use _ or default_server only if you want a catch-all.

Tip: include both apex and www or any aliases you want.

location / { ... }

Means: rules for any request path starting with /. This is typically used to proxy all traffic.

What to mention: keep / to proxy entire site, or use /artifactory/ if you only want a subpath.

proxy_pass http://localhost:8081;

Means: forward incoming requests to the upstream server at http://localhost:8081.

What to mention / replace with:

If Artifactory runs on same machine and listens on 8081: http://127.0.0.1:8081; or http://localhost:8081;

If it’s on another host: http://10.0.0.5:8081; or use an upstream block with a name.

If your Artifactory context path is /artifactory/ and you want to keep paths exact, be careful with trailing slash differences (see note below).

Important: trailing slash behavior:

proxy_pass http://localhost:8081; preserves the full request URI (no rewrite).

proxy_pass http://localhost:8081/; rewrites the matched location prefix. Choose what you need.

proxy_set_header Host $host;

Means: set the Host header sent to the backend to the original requested host (e.g. repo.example.com).

What to mention: usually you want the frontend host to reach backend so the backend can generate correct absolute URLs and for virtual-hosted services.

Alternative: proxy_set_header Host $proxy_host; or hardcode artifactory.internal:8081 if required.

proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;

Means: forward client IP (the immediate remote IP) to the backend in X-Real-IP.

What to mention: useful for logging on Artifactory so it knows the client’s IP rather than the proxy’s IP.

proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;

Means: append the client IP to the X-Forwarded-For header chain (keeps previous proxy IPs too).

What to mention: standard header used to track original client IPs through multiple proxies.

proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;

Means: sends http or https (value of $scheme) to backend in X-Forwarded-Proto.

What to mention: Artifactory (and many web apps) use this to know the original protocol so it can generate correct https:// links and redirects.

